{"name":"Napoleon","hex":"#404149","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Napoleon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Napoleon Bonaparte (1769–1821), a French military commander and political leader.","A male given name from Italian sometimes given in honor of the French emperor."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of napoleon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Napoleon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Napoleon","blocks":[{"text":"Napoleon Bonaparte, later known by his regnal name Napoleon I, was Emperor of the French from 18 May 1804 until his first abdication in 1814, with a brief restoration during the Hundred Days in 1815. He rose to prominence as a general during the French Revolution and led a series of military campaigns across Europe and the Middle East during the French Revolutionary and Napoleonic Wars. As a statesman, he implemented numerous legal and administrative reforms in France and Europe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Jacques-Louis_David_-_The_Emperor_Napoleon_in_His_Study_at_the_Tuileries_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/330px-Jacques-Louis_David_-_The_Emperor_Napoleon_in_His_Study_at_the_Tuileries_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napoleon","wikidata":"Q517"},{"title":"Napoleon (2023 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Napoleon is a 2023 epic historical war film directed and co-produced by Ridley Scott from a screenplay by David Scarpa. Based on the life of Napoleon and primarily depicting his rise to power, as well as his relationship with his wife, Joséphine, it stars Joaquin Phoenix as Napoleon and Vanessa Kirby as Joséphine."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2e/Napoleon_Film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napoleon_(2023_film)","wikidata":"Q105806948"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Carlo_Buonaparte.jpg/500px-Carlo_Buonaparte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Carlo_Buonaparte.jpg/1280px-Carlo_Buonaparte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Carlo_Buonaparte.jpg/500px-Carlo_Buonaparte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Napoleon's father, Carlo Buonaparte, fought for Corsican independence under Pasquale Paoli. After their defeat, he eventually became the island's representative to Louis XVI's court.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarlo_Buonaparte.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Henri_F%C3%A9lix_Emmanuel_Philippoteaux_-_Portrait_of_Napoleon_Bonaparte.jpg/500px-Henri_F%C3%A9lix_Emmanuel_Philippoteaux_-_Portrait_of_Napoleon_Bonaparte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Henri_F%C3%A9lix_Emmanuel_Philippoteaux_-_Portrait_of_Napoleon_Bonaparte.jpg/500px-Henri_F%C3%A9lix_Emmanuel_Philippoteaux_-_Portrait_of_Napoleon_Bonaparte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bonaparte, aged 23, as lieutenant-colonel of a battalion of Corsican Republican volunteers. Portrait made in 1835 by Henri Félix Emmanuel Philippoteaux.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHenri_F%C3%A9lix_Emmanuel_Philippoteaux_-_Portrait_of_Napoleon_Bonaparte.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Napoleon_%C3%A0_Toulon_par_Edouard_Detaille.jpg/500px-Napoleon_%C3%A0_Toulon_par_Edouard_Detaille.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe